Give this build its own bundle identifier: bar.esko.Ghostty

This build is signed differently from the official one, so it must not
claim com.mitchellh.ghostty. Launch Services and privacy permissions
(TCC) key on the bundle identifier. With two apps under one identifier
and different signatures, Launch Services may open either one, and a
permission recorded for one fails the signature check for the other.

Change the identity macOS sees: the app's PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER in
all three configurations, the dock tile plugin's, and the defaults suite
the plugin reads the custom icon from (the app's own defaults domain).

Ghostty's own namespace stays: build_config.bundle_id still names the
Application Support and cache folders, the translation domain (the .mo
files are built under that name) and the Zig log subsystem. Notification,
pasteboard and type names stay too; they are strings, not identity.

--- a/macos/Ghostty.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
+++ b/macos/Ghostty.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
@@ -765,7 +765,7 @@
 				MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 13.0;
 				MARKETING_VERSION = 0.1;
 				"OTHER_LDFLAGS[arch=*]" = "-lstdc++";
-				PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.mitchellh.ghostty;
+				PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = bar.esko.Ghostty;
 				PRODUCT_NAME = "$(TARGET_NAME)";
 				SWIFT_EMIT_LOC_STRINGS = YES;
